    "body": "Release gate run 43739171721: one step failed, `app heavy: pocket3d_hsm`.\n\n**What failed.** The test `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` failed at `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs:99`. This is the assert from #850, which says that no planning budget refuses a level. The path notes said these things:\n- At Z 15 and Z 5, the HSM plan went past its growth budget.\n- At Z 10, it would post 124740 moves.\n- At Z 0, it left 22% of the area uncut.\n\nAt those levels, Offset rings cut the level and the notes say so. The worst corner scallop is at (34.99, -34.99), which is the stock corner and not a point in the bore. The test also fails the same way on Windows, so the failure does not depend on the OS.\n\n**Why.** PR #1780 (#1774) makes a whole-model 3D Pocket clear the stock around the model out to the stock outline. That change is intended and reviewed. The test uses a 70 x 70 block around the 60 mm part. Each level is now a wide ring with the part as an island, and not only the bore that the test pins. The fallbacks are visible in the notes and the path verifies clean. The product is correct, and the test fixture is stale.\n\n**What commit bf752be65 changes.** Only the test changes. Before it generates, the test sets Tool containment: Inside on the operation with one `EditOperationParams::with_area` command. Inside is the native containment of a pocket, so the area law returns the part silhouette unchanged. A controlled region does not get the open-side growth. No assert changed, and the `#[test]` count stays at 2.\n\n**Readings (Windows x86_64, release).**\n- Before the commit: the test fails at line 99 (budget notes at Z 15 and Z 5).\n- After the commit: (16017, 15360, 1427). This is the exact triple pinned for #1402. There is no budget note and no fallback.\n\nThe Linux triple (16029, 15372, 1427) was not measured again on Linux. The next cut gate run will check it.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
